---
import Base from "../../layouts/Base.astro";
import DocsSidebar from "../../components/DocsSidebar.astro";

const table = [
  { name: "@g2w/core", role: "Renderer-agnostic contracts: Game, SceneManager, InputState, GamepadState, AssetManager, Sprite2D/Transform2D, audio contract.", deps: "none", status: "done" },
  { name: "@g2w/runtime", role: "Effect-based application runtime: managed lifecycle scope, G2WGame with idempotent shutdown and LIFO finalizers.", deps: "core, effect", status: "done" },
  { name: "@g2w/renderer-pixi", role: "PixiJS 8 renderer adapter: WebGL/Canvas/WebGPU backends, sprite views, texture asset loading.", deps: "core, pixi.js", status: "done" },
  { name: "@g2w/input-dom", role: "DOM adapter: keyboard, pointer, and multi-touch through Pointer Events onto InputState.", deps: "core", status: "done" },
  { name: "@g2w/input-gamepad", role: "Gamepad API adapter with an injectable polling source; the host drives poll() once per frame.", deps: "core", status: "done" },
  { name: "@g2w/audio-web", role: "Web Audio backend: decodes sound files, starts playbacks, owns the AudioContext lifecycle.", deps: "core", status: "done" },
  { name: "@g2w/devtools", role: "Read-only dev overlay: scene explorer, transforms, FPS, watched input, runtime logs. Dev-only.", deps: "core", status: "done" },
  { name: "create-g2w", role: "Zero-dependency CLI that scaffolds a TypeScript + Vite game project from a bundled template.", deps: "none", status: "done" },
  { name: "@g2w/renderer-three", role: "Planned 3D rendering adapter proving the renderer contract generalizes.", deps: "core, three", status: "planned" },
];
---

<Base title="Packages · g2w docs">
  <div class="docs">
    <DocsSidebar active="pkg-core" />

    <main class="docs-main prose">
      <div class="crumb">docs / packages</div>
      <h1>Packages</h1>
      <p>
        g2w is not one big framework — it is a set of small packages with one strict
        rule, enforced by architecture tests: adapters depend on
        <code>@g2w/core</code>, and core never depends back. You compose only what
        your game needs.
      </p>

      <h2 id="table">The full list</h2>
      <div class="pkg-table" style="box-shadow: none">
        <table>
          <thead>
            <tr><th>Package</th><th>Responsibility</th><th>Status</th></tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            {table.map((row) => (
              <tr>
                <td class="name"><code>{row.name}</code></td>
                <td class="desc">{row.role}</td>
                <td>{row.status === "done" ? <span class="badge done">done</span> : <span class="badge planned">planned</span>}</td>
              </tr>
            ))}
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>

      <h2 id="core">@g2w/core — the contract layer</h2>
      <p>
        Everything renderer-agnostic lives here, and it has <b>zero runtime
        dependencies</b> — it never imports a rendering technology and never touches
        browser globals or DOM events at runtime. Inside you find the
        <code>Game</code> state machine and frame loop, the renderer contract and
        <code>SceneManager</code>, the DOM-free <code>InputState</code> /
        <code>GamepadState</code>, the generic <code>AssetManager</code>, the
        <code>Transform2D</code>/<code>Sprite2D</code>/<code>Anchor2D</code> model,
        the <code>GameObject</code> layer, and the <code>AudioManager</code>
        contract.
      </p>

      <h2 id="runtime">@g2w/runtime — the Effect layer</h2>
      <p>
        The primary application path. One managed Effect runtime orchestrates the
        core <code>Game</code> lifecycle as <code>G2WGame</code>: renderer init as a
        lifecycle effect, ownership as LIFO finalizers, idempotent disposal, and
        best-effort cleanup whose failures stay observable. The frame hot path never
        allocates an Effect runtime, effect, or promise — the per-frame update is a
        plain synchronous call. Core's <code>Game</code> ships side by side as the
        reference implementation and stays Effect-free.
      </p>

      <h2 id="adapters">Adapters — browser concerns live at the edge</h2>
      <p>
        Each adapter implements one core contract and may depend only on
        <code>@g2w/core</code> (plus its technology, for the renderer):
      </p>
      <p>
        <code>@g2w/renderer-pixi</code> adapts PixiJS 8 and adds texture loading
        plus <code>createSpriteView</code>.
        <code>@g2w/input-dom</code> and <code>@g2w/input-gamepad</code> feed
        normalized events and sampled state into core.
        <code>@g2w/audio-web</code> implements the audio backend on Web Audio.
        <code>@g2w/devtools</code> observes through immutable snapshots and never
        mutates the runtime.
      </p>

      <h2 id="cli">create-g2w — a developer tool, not a runtime</h2>
      <p>
        A zero-dependency Node CLI (Node ≥ 22) that scaffolds a game from its
        bundled template. It imports nothing from g2w, never prompts, and its only
        subprocess is a local <code>git init</code>. See
        <a href="/docs/installation">Installation</a>.
      </p>

      <h2 id="status">Publishing status</h2>
      <div class="callout" style="box-shadow: none">
        <span class="tag">Status</span>
        <span>
          <b>All eight packages are published to npm at 0.1.0</b> (released
          2026-10-28 via OIDC trusted publishing from the manual release workflow).
          This is an early 0.x release: the public API may still change before 1.0
          (Roadmap risk: semver stability).
        </span>
      </div>

      <h2 id="footprint">Dependency footprint</h2>
      <p>
        Verified sizes from the npm registry and a fresh <code>npm install</code>
        (2026-10-29), so you can pick the composition that fits your budget:
      </p>
      <div class="pkg-table" style="box-shadow: none">
        <table>
          <thead>
            <tr><th>Composition</th><th>node_modules</th><th>Browser bundle (gzip)</th></tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr>
              <td class="name">@g2w/core only</td>
              <td>~0.2 MB</td>
              <td>~1 KB — the core contract is dependency-free</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td class="name">g2w set (core + runtime + renderer-pixi + input-dom)</td>
              <td>~131 MB</td>
              <td>~209 KB (the hello-world demo build)</td>
            </tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
      <p>
        Where the disk weight comes from, measured on the same install: the
        <code>@g2w/*</code> packages themselves are <b>~0.3 MB</b>; the rest is
        their declared dependencies — <b>pixi.js ~73 MB</b> (the renderer) and
        <b>effect ~51 MB</b> (@g2w/runtime). The browser bundle tells the
        opposite story: tree-shaking keeps Effect's share small (the demo's
        total shipped JavaScript is ~209 KB gzipped, and Effect added only
        ~82 KB raw when it landed in E4), while the renderer dominates what a
        player actually downloads.
      </p>
      <div class="callout" style="box-shadow: none">
        <span class="tag">Trade-off</span>
        <span>
          <b>Effect costs ~51 MB on disk but ~tens of KB in the browser.</b> It is
          paid once at install time by developers, not by players. If a minimal
          install matters more than the Effect-native <code>G2WGame</code>
          lifecycle, skip <code>@g2w/runtime</code> and boot the core
          <code>Game</code> directly — that path carries zero Effect weight, and
          <code>@g2w/core</code> is architecturally guaranteed to stay
          Effect-free. This balance was evaluated in October 2026; it is
          re-checked when the benchmark harness lands.
        </span>
      </div>

      <h2 id="next">Next steps</h2>
      <p>
        Read the <a href="/docs/introduction#lifecycle">game lifecycle</a> states,
        or the
        <a href="https://github.com/AlexanderDev2004/g2w/blob/main/ARCHITECTURE.md"
          >architecture notes</a
        > for the boundary rules each test enforces.
      </p>
    </main>

    <aside class="docs-toc">
      <div class="ttl">On this page</div>
      <a class="on" href="#">Packages</a>
      <a href="#table">The full list</a>
      <a href="#core">@g2w/core</a>
      <a href="#runtime">@g2w/runtime</a>
      <a href="#adapters">Adapters</a>
      <a href="#cli">create-g2w</a>
      <a href="#status">Publishing status</a>
      <a href="#footprint">Dependency footprint</a>
      <a href="#next">Next steps</a>
    </aside>
  </div>
</Base>

<style>
  .badge {
    display: inline-block;
    font-family: var(--mono);
    font-size: 10.5px;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    padding: 2px 8px;
    border: 1.5px solid var(--ink);
  }
  .badge.done {
    background: var(--ink);
    color: var(--paper);
  }
  .badge.planned {
    background: transparent;
    color: var(--ink-60);
    border-color: var(--line);
  }
</style>
